// expect-error: NITPICK-RESOLVE-012
// expect-error-at: 11:1
//
// The workbench's DEF-2 (OPEN_DECISIONS §2f; their O-N8): a root file whose
// `mod:` names a SIBLING that exists. Until D-248 the loader read the header
// as an import, loaded `header_sibling.npk`, merged both files into one
// program and emitted two `@main` at exit 0, which `llc` then refused. Now
// the header is refused where it stands and the sibling is NOT loaded -- its
// own `main` would be RESOLVE-013 under step 1's entry-point rule, and D-237's
// exact set proves no second diagnostic appears.
mod:header_sibling;
func:main = int32(cstring[]:_~argv) { exit 1i32; };
func:failsafe = int32(Error:e) { exit 9i32; };
